Experiment: Sending E-mail and SMS Using Mobile Application (Android)
Aim
To develop an Android mobile application that enables the user to send E-mail and SMS using Android Intents. The application opens the default E-mail or SMS application with the recipient details and message content pre-filled. Android provides ACTION_SENDTO intents with mailto: and smsto: schemes for these tasks. 
________________________________________
Algorithm
For Sending E-mail
1.	Start the application. 
2.	Enter the recipient E-mail address. 
3.	Enter the subject and message. 
4.	Click the Send E-mail button. 
5.	Create an Intent using Intent.ACTION_SENDTO. 
6.	Set the URI as mailto:. 
7.	Add recipient, subject, and message as extras. 
8.	Launch the E-mail application. 
9.	User sends the E-mail. 
10.	Stop. 
For Sending SMS
1.	Start the application. 
2.	Enter the recipient mobile number. 
3.	Enter the SMS message. 
4.	Click the Send SMS button. 
5.	Create an Intent using Intent.ACTION_SENDTO. 
6.	Set the URI as smsto:. 
7.	Attach the SMS body. 
8.	Launch the default SMS application. 
9.	User sends the SMS. 
10.	Stop. 
________________________________________
Kotlin Code
MainActivity.kt
package com.example.emailsmsapp

import android.content.Intent
import android.net.Uri
import android.os.Bundle
import android.widget.Button
import androidx.appcompat.app.AppCompatActivity

class MainActivity : AppCompatActivity() {

    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
        setContentView(R.layout.activity_main)

        val emailButton = findViewById<Button>(R.id.btnEmail)
        val smsButton = findViewById<Button>(R.id.btnSMS)

        emailButton.setOnClickListener {

            val intent = Intent(Intent.ACTION_SENDTO)
            intent.data = Uri.parse("mailto:")
            intent.putExtra(
                Intent.EXTRA_EMAIL,
                arrayOf("receiver@gmail.com")
            )
            intent.putExtra(
                Intent.EXTRA_SUBJECT,
                "Android Mail"
            )
            intent.putExtra(
                Intent.EXTRA_TEXT,
                "This mail is sent from Android Application."
            )

            startActivity(intent)
        }

        smsButton.setOnClickListener {

            val intent = Intent(Intent.ACTION_SENDTO)
            intent.data = Uri.parse("smsto:9876543210")
            intent.putExtra(
                "sms_body",
                "Hello! Message from Android Application."
            )

            startActivity(intent)
        }
    }
}
